## Smell-Free Patterns ✓

`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException` (line 155) is exemplary:
- Uses `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` — no manual `try`/`catch`
- Asserts on a specific property (`ParamName`), not `ToString()`
- Single responsibility — tests exactly one behavior
- No magic numbers, no external dependencies, no sleeps

